From fdf01c05846fc07480b83cd17632f779e99d3ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luo Jie <luoj@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:46:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: nsscc-qca8k: Use prepare ops for RCG clocks

The QCA8K NSSCC registers are accessed over MDIO, which takes a mutex
and sleeps. The RCG clocks use clk_rcg2_ops and clk_rcg2_fm_ops, whose
.is_enabled reads the hardware. clk_disable_unused() calls it with the
enable spinlock held and IRQs disabled, which leads to sleeping in
atomic context when the driver probes before late_initcall_sync.

Switch the RCG clocks to clk_rcg2_prepare_ops and
clk_rcg2_fm_prepare_ops, so the hardware status is read only from
sleepable context.

Fixes: 79025754e62b ("clk: qcom: add clock controller driver for qca8386/qca8084")

Change-Id: I2cc0f9cd9114411960a9934a0c4257e9cedab0a2
Signed-off-by: Luo Jie <luoj@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
